From 33320b424aebd349ef84c03f7f05998ac6d11f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Reilly <jreilly1821@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 06:05:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Device-list updates: m.device_list_update,
 device_lists.changed, /keys/changes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A peer who reinstalls the app is a new device with new keys. Until now
nothing told the other phones, so they kept encrypting to the device
that was gone.

- Every `/keys/upload` carrying device keys is a device-list change: the
  user's `stream_id` advances — persisted in a new `device_streams` table
  (schema v6), so a restart cannot replay an old one — and an
  `m.device_list_update` EDU goes through the durable outbox to every
  server sharing a room with the user, the same path as room keys.
- Inbound updates for a peer's user land in a change log; one naming a
  user we own is dropped. Each sliding-sync connection remembers where it
  last read the log and reports the users after that under
  `extensions.e2ee.device_lists.changed`, filtered to those sharing a
  room with the caller, and a change wakes a waiting long-poll. Legacy
  `/sync` carries the same under the top-level `device_lists`, and its
  real one-time key counts.
- `GET /keys/changes` answers with every user sharing a room whose
  devices have changed at all: a superset of the exact answer, since
  legacy tokens carry no device-log coordinate, and safe, because the
  only thing a client does with the list is fetch keys again.
- The federation `GET /user/devices/{user}` reports the real stream id.
- A login that names a device gets that device; one that names none
  gets a fresh id under the multi-user shim and the conventional id in
  the single-user build.

Complement: `TestKeyChangesLocal` added to the allowlist.
`TestDeviceListUpdates` is left out — its local subtests want
`device_lists.changed`/`left` to follow room membership, which this
server does not derive.

